\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Baseline train/validation accuracy under the three schedules: (a) $10^{-3}$/patience~$7$, (b) $10^{-4}$/patience~$5$, both on non-overlapping windows, and (c) $10^{-3}$/patience~$12$ on sliding windows. In (a) the training curve detaches from the validation one after $\approx \!6$ epochs (overfitting the single environment); in (b) the two stay glued together and stop \emph  {under}-fitted at $0.575$, and yet generalize better; in (c) the denser windows let the model reach $0.756$ with validation accuracy $12$ points above (a).}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
